<article class="env-lemma" id="067J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/067J">Lemma <span data-tag="067J">15.84.4</span>.</a> A ring map which is flat and of finite presentation is perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $A \to B$ be a ring map which is flat and of finite presentation. It is clear that $B$ has finite tor dimension. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JO" data-tag="02JO">10.168.1</a> there exists a finite type $\mathbf{Z}$-algebra $A_0 \subset A$ and a flat finite type ring map $A_0 \to B_0$ such that $B = B_0 \otimes _{A_0} A$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/067F" data-tag="067F">15.83.17</a> we see that $A_0 \to B_0$ is pseudo-coherent. As $A_0 \to B_0$ is flat we see that $B_0$ and $A$ are tor independent over $A_0$, hence we may use Lemma <a href="/tag/067A" data-tag="067A">15.83.12</a> to conclude that $A \to B$ is pseudo-coherent. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>